  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "He enters the story during the Gu Yue Awakening Ceremony on Qing Mao Mountain, where the clan stands after its migration into the South Border. He is named Gu Yue Mo Bei’s grandfather, is horse-faced, and stands against his old rival Gu Yue Chi Lian among the watching elders. Fang Yuan’s narration in that scene already treats the two as the clan’s two biggest influential authorities.",
      "chapters": [
        4
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_awakening_ceremony",
        "loc_qing_mao_mountain",
        "char_gu_yue_mo_bei",
        "char_gu_yue_chi_lian",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is a horse-faced elder.",
      "chapters": [
        4
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Inside the Gu Yue clan, power sits in three camps: the clan leader’s side, Gu Yue Chi Lian’s Chi family, and Gu Yue Mo Chen’s Mo family.",
      "chapters": [
        78
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mo-family-head",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_yue_clan",
        "fac_chi_family",
        "fac_mo_family"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Early dialogue calls that camp the Mo family branch and treats Mo Chen as the master who expects Mo Bei to take charge of it against the Chi family branch.",
      "chapters": [
        21
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mo-family-head",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Later wording names the same camp the Mo faction, with Mo Bei as its future leader beside Chi Cheng on the Chi side.",
      "chapters": [
        83
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mo-family-head",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gu_yue_chi_cheng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is already a clan elder of high authority when the novel opens.",
      "chapters": [
        4
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mo-family-head",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He and Chi Lian sit as the authoritative elders under clan leader Gu Yue Bo at the year-end examination tent.",
      "chapters": [
        82
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mo-family-head",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gu_yue_bo"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later wording names the two of them as the head of the clan elders when Bo presses a reward past their grim faces.",
      "chapters": [
        86
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mo-family-head",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After Fang Zheng’s A grade result he even contests Chi Lian for the right to raise the boy, before Gu Yue Bo takes that claim himself.",
      "chapters": [
        6
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mo-family-head",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_zheng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "His recorded household centres on two grandchildren. Mo Bei is the male heir he plans around.",
      "chapters": [
        21
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rules-grandchildren-and-gao-wan",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu Yue Mo Yan is the granddaughter who enters his study without knocking and reports on wolf dens for him. In that study scene he tells her not to interfere in junior fights, because breaking that rule would look like Mo family bullying.",
      "chapters": [
        31
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rules-grandchildren-and-gao-wan",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gu_yue_mo_yan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Fang Yuan kills the Mo family servant Gao Wan and leaves a minced corpse at the back door, Mo Chen appears as the family elder who reads the box as both compromise and threat. He confines Mo Yan for seven days, compensates Fang Yuan with thirty primeval stones, and pays Gao Wan’s family fifty before expelling them, all to protect the family’s reputation rather than pursue a junior fight into elder interference.",
      "chapters": [
        37
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rules-grandchildren-and-gao-wan",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gao_wan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan’s own reading of that choice is that Mo Chen fears setting a precedent that could later fall on Mo Bei, the family’s only male line.",
      "chapters": [
        38
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rules-grandchildren-and-gao-wan",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Political enmity with Chi Lian does not erase shared village interest. When a River Swallowing Toad threatens Qing Mao Mountain, Mo Chen backs Chi Lian’s urgency and sets aside past prejudice for the crisis.",
      "chapters": [
        117
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rules-grandchildren-and-gao-wan",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_river_swallowing_toad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "By clan system, Gu Masters who advance to rank three become new elders. Mo Chen is already seated among those elders when Fang Yuan’s rank three advance reshuffles the hall, and he privately regrets not recruiting Fang Yuan earlier.",
      "chapters": [
        153
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rank-three-standing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "During the wolf tide he is heavily injured and spends two weeks recuperating in a private room. That absence keeps him off the thunder crown wolf assault in which Chi Lian dies, and he forces himself to the later banquet for Tie Xue Leng while still pale and hurt.",
      "chapters": [
        171
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "wolf-tide-aftermath",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tie_xue_leng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The same stretch records that Mo Bei has already died in the wolf tide, leaving the Mo faction without an inheritor under clan rules that favour male succession.",
      "chapters": [
        172
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "wolf-tide-aftermath",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "That injury ends his rank three cultivation. He was formerly rank three and has fallen to rank two with no chance of regaining rank three. He hides the drop with a Gu worm while knowing exposure will cost him clan elder status. At the banquet he publicly takes blame for Fang Yuan missing the battlefield, claiming he knocked Fang Yuan out for Mo Yan’s sake, and offers to accept stripping of elder status. The cover is stretched and hard for the other elders to believe, but it shields Fang Yuan and spends Mo Chen’s own reputation to do it.",
      "chapters": [
        172
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "wolf-tide-aftermath",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Afterward he presses Fang Yuan as the son-in-law who could inherit Mo faction assets through marriage to Mo Yan.",
      "chapters": [
        172
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "wolf-tide-aftermath",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan answers with extreme bride-price demands and is thrown out.",
      "chapters": [
        174
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "wolf-tide-aftermath",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the same elder stretch Yao Ji tries to push Mo Chen toward a Xiong clan mission, and he refuses by naming her greater fame and seniority.",
      "chapters": [
        175
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "wolf-tide-aftermath",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_xiong_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He returns when Yao faction pressure and the coming rank two reveal leave Mo Chen no better option. They settle on a cut price with forty thousand primeval stones in advance, a Pig Iron Gu, and an Afterlife Grass Gu Mo Chen claims not to have on hand in the Mo faction warehouse. Mo Yan accepts the marriage as a family sacrifice while still hating Fang Yuan.",
      "chapters": [
        176
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "wolf-tide-aftermath",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_pig_iron_gu",
        "gu_afterlife_grass_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan later records that he has received the Pig Iron Gu and the full forty thousand stones, with only the healing grass still unpaid when he abandons waiting for it.",
      "chapters": [
        180
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "wolf-tide-aftermath",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He still counts those forty thousand among the stones thrown into Heavenly Essence Treasure Lotus work.",
      "chapters": [
        182
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "wolf-tide-aftermath",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_heavenly_essence_treasure_lotus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The fan translation writes the name as Gu Yue Mo Chen, with Elder Mo Chen and Lord Mo Chen as respectful short forms in clan speech.",
      "chapters": [
        175
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "translation-notes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The camp under him is called Mo family, Mo family branch, and Mo faction in different chapters, with no change of membership implied.",
      "chapters": [
        21
      ],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "translation-notes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "A few early academy scenes also print “Gu Yue Mo Chen” where the surrounding action is clearly the student heir Mo Bei rather than the elder, which is a translation slip rather than a second person.",
      "chapters": [
        43
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "translation-notes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "No Chinese characters for his personal name appear in the English chapter text used here.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "translation-notes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
